'Base.Relics.HeirloomSealOfTheRealm_DescØTo reign over China was to hold the Heirloom Seal of the Realm - a single block of lustrous jade carved with the authority of Heaven itself. Commissioned for Qin Shi Huang, the first Emperor of China, its inscription declared the divine right to rule: ‚ÄúHaving received the Mandate of Heaven, may the emperor lead a long and prosperous life.‚Äù For centuries, each dynasty's legitimacy flowed through this seal, pressed upon edicts and decrees as a symbol of celestial endorsement.<br><br>Guarded in the Forbidden City and passed from emperor to emperor, the Seal was more than a signature; it was a claim to the very heart of an empire. Ambassadors bowed before it, conspiracies brewed to seize it, and its mark, stamped in vermillion, sent ripples across nations. Long sought by warlords and revered by scholars, the Heirloom Seal remains a touchstone of imperial history - a jade artifact that once made (and unmade) the fate of dynasties.
