Base.Units.Unit_LudwigII_Descè	Dream in stone and gold with Ludwig II, the Fairy Tale King of Bavaria! This visionary 19th century monarch ascended the throne at just 18, and turned the Bavarian Alps into a canvas for some of the most breathtaking palaces ever conceived. A devoted patron of the composer Richard Wagner, Ludwig rescued him from financial ruin and changed the course of music history forever.<br><br>Ludwig's grandest legacy is written in stone across Bavaria: the palaces of Neuschwanstein, Linderhof, and Herrenchiemsee. Neuschwanstein, perched upon a crag and adorned with scenes from Wagner's operas, has become one of the most iconic castles on the planet, a global symbol of fantasy that has inspired countless fairy tale castles in film and popular culture. Yet Ludwig was no mere dreamer: his castles featured cutting-edge technology, from central heating to automatic flushing toilets, and Linderhof's Venus Grotto housed Bavaria's first electricity plant.<br><br>Though deposed in 1886 amid controversy, his mysterious death only deepened his legend. The poet Paul Verlaine called him 'the only true king of this century', and Bavarians still lovingly call him 'the Kini'.e
