$Base.Units.Unit_GiacomoCasanova_DescÍ	Charm your way through history with Giacomo Casanova, the legendary Venetian adventurer whose name became synonymous with romance! This 18th-century polymath lived a thousand lives in one - gambler, spy, alchemist, playwright, violinist, and most famously, history's greatest lover. His autobiography chronicles encounters with over 120 lovers, but Casanova was far more than just a seducer.<br><br>Born in Venice, Casanova traveled across Europe's royal courts, debating with Voltaire, dining with Catherine the Great, and escaping from Venice's inescapable Leads prison by climbing through the roof. He spoke multiple languages, wrote philosophy and mathematics, and translated Homer's Iliad. His greatest talent wasn't seduction but conversation - he could enchant anyone from servants to sovereigns.<br><br>Though remembered primarily for his romantic exploits, Casanova was a true Enlightenment figure who lived by wit and charm in an age of rigid social hierarchy. He ended his days as a librarian in Bohemia, writing his memoirs that would scandalize and captivate readers for centuries. In Heroes of History, he's been trying to charm various heroes with mixed results - Lagertha nearly threw him off a cliff, but somehow he talked his way out of it!º
