Base.Units.Unit_ZhengYiSao_DescúKneel before the code, or find your head separated from your neck, for Zheng Yi Sao has joined the Heroes of History! Rising from the flower boats of Canton to absolute dominion over the South China Sea, this Pirate Queen of history ruled a floating confederation that rivaled empires, answering neither to the Qing Emperor nor any European admiral. Renowned for her terrifying organizational genius rather than supernatural gifts, she commanded the allegiance of tens of thousands of outlaws through sheer iron will.<br><br>Her most famous legend is not one of myth, but of cold, historical reality. At the height of her power, controlling the massive Red Flag Fleet, she baffled and defeated the combined naval forces of China, Britain, and Portugal. Yet, her greatest victory was diplomatic. Recognizing the shifting tides, she managed to persuade the Chinese government to accept her surrender on her own terms, allowing her to keep her loot and retire a free, wealthy woman with a naval title.<br><br>What set Zheng Yi Sao apart was her disciplined chaos. Unlike typical, unruly pirate crews, she enforced a brutal, unwavering code of laws‚Äîimposing immediate execution for disobedience or stealing from the common fund. She carved her own path using administrative brilliance, business acumen, and a ruthlessness that cut when weaponized. Once overshadowed by Western tales of piracy, she has been reclaimed by modern interpretations as perhaps the most successful pirate captain of all time: a woman who built an empire on the waves and answered to no one.:
